block head
    title Anemia - Plants Cause Disease

block content
    h1 Anemia
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/anemia/symptoms-causes/syc-20351360") Mayo Clinic]:
    blockquote Anemia is a problem of not having enough healthy red blood cells or hemoglobin to carry oxygen to the body's tissues. Hemoglobin is a protein found in red cells that carries oxygen from the lungs to all other organs in the body. Having anemia can cause tiredness, weakness and shortness of breath.
